Slice 050d, `tln tool remove talon --remove-tools` on Windows: the files of the tools (R-ST10, R-RM8, R-B6, R-ST6, R-ST11). The fake machine is `os=windows arch=x64`. The bin dir of Windows is `<USERPROFILE>\.local\bin`: the dir `u<n>\.local\bin` (a name with `\`) in the home. One home for each run (`HOME` and `USERPROFILE` are `{w}/home/u<n>`), no compiler. `CI=true` (no person: option 2 by the flag). `fx/random` is not set, so every `random!` gives `0123456789abcdef`.
`tools.json` has `talon` and 4 tools. `foo` has its data file and an entry that is Talon's (the same text). `bar` has its data file and an entry that the user made (another text: kept, R-ST6). `baz` has its data file and no entry. `qux` has no file at all (a manifest entry whose files are gone). Talon has `tln.exe` and `roc.exe` in the bin dir and `tln.exe` in the data bin dir. The fake `rename` says `Exists` for a target that ends with `u2\.local\bin/foo.0123456789abcdef.del`.

| Run | Home | Words | Result | Rules |
| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |
| 1 | u1 | `tool rm talon --remove-tools` | under the lock of `tools.json`: one `random!`, then `rename!` of the files of the tools to `<name>.0123456789abcdef.del`, in the order of `Del.removed` for each tool in the order of `tools.json`: the entry `foo.exe`, the data file `foo.exe`, the data file `bar.exe`, the data file `baz.exe` (the entry of `bar` is not Talon's, `baz` has no entry, `qux` has no file: no rename of a missing file). No `delete!` of a tool file. `tools.json` is deleted. The `Path` step, the data of Talon, then the files of Talon are renamed (one more `random!`). The one detached cleanup has the 4 `.del` files of the tools first, then the 3 of Talon (`TALON_DEL_1` to `TALON_DEL_7`). The entry of `bar` stays, with the warning | R-ST10, R-RM8, R-RM5, R-ST6, R-ST11 |
| 2 | u2 | `tool rm talon --remove-tools` | the first rename (the entry `foo.exe` to `foo.0123456789abcdef.del`) gives `Exists`: exit 18 `cannot move <from> to <to>: Exists`. Nothing is renamed, `tools.json` and the files of the tools stay, no `Path` change, no rename of a file of Talon, no cleanup. Talon is last, so it is still installed and the command can run again | R-ST10, R-EC18, R-RM5, Q-R1 |

Each run starts with the sweep of the `.del` files (`env_all` and one `list_dirs` of the 2 dirs, no `.del` file, so no `delete`).
